cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "RegioInvest Wind: A model for regional onshore wind investment in Germany"
message: "If you use this code, please cite the associated paper and this software."
type: software

authors:
  - family-names: "Pflugfelder"
    given-names: "Yannik"
    affiliation: "University of Duisburg-Essen, House of Energy, Climate and Finance"

version: "v1.0"
date-released: 2026-04-22

repository-code: "https://github.com/PfluYa/Regio_Invest_Wind_open"

abstract: >
  RegioInvest Wind is a MATLAB-based model for simulating regional onshore wind 
  power deployment in Germany. The model allocates future capacity expansion 
  across regions and turbine types under different policy scenarios, combining 
  spatial constraints, investment decisions, and wind resource modeling.

keywords:
  - wind energy
  - investment modeling
  - discrete choice
  - spatial allocation
  - energy policy

license: MIT

